From 6ee0d76e987ab5a13a64032582bc3da945ce3eae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:35:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tilelang): gather column shards directly into serving
 buffers

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus candidate-38 (1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4).

The compressor materializes concatenated gathered columns before copying them into its value/gate buffers. Sharded vision additionally copies unpadded column slices. Gather rank-major rows and fuse layout conversion, unpadding and final stores into one TileLang launch. Preserve exact payload bits, output ownership and stream order. Validate layouts explicitly and declare both scalar and aligned-vector kernels before cache freeze.

Quality: no projection or accumulation arithmetic changes. Collective payload bytes are unchanged; requested gather layout changes to dim zero and still requires distributed serving qualification. Tests cover independent concatenation, one/two outputs, topology widths, tails, striding, NaN/signed-zero bits, poisoned padding, large row grids and CUDA replay. Native receipts are retained with the deployment experiment. Upstream status: local candidate, not submitted.
